# 61. One Very Important Concept: Candidate Generation vs Ranking

Modern search systems often separate these two.

## Candidate generation

Find things that **could** be matches.

For example:

```text
query = recieve
```

Generate:

```text
receive
receiver
recipe
```

Methods:

```text
Levenshtein automaton
BK-tree
SymSpell
```

---

## Ranking

Now decide which candidate is best.

Possible signals:

```text
edit distance
word frequency
Jaro-Winkler
language model probability
context
document frequency
query likelihood
```

So:

```text
                   QUERY
                     │
                     ▼
             Candidate generation
                     │
          ┌──────────┼─────────┐
          ▼          ▼         ▼
       receive    recipe    receiver
          │          │         │
          └──────────┼─────────┘
                     ▼
                   ranking
                     │
                     ▼
                  receive
```

This distinction is extremely important in real search engines.

