# 62. How I'd Remember Each One

### Levenshtein

> **How many insert/delete/substitute operations?**

```text
cat → cut = 1
```

### Damerau-Levenshtein

> **Levenshtein + adjacent swap**

```text
teh → the = 1
```

### Hamming

> **How many positions differ?**

```text
10110
10010
  ↑
= 1
```

### Needleman-Wunsch

> **Align the entire sequences**

```text
GLOBAL
```

### Smith-Waterman

> **Find the best matching region**

```text
LOCAL
```

### Jaro

> **How well do characters match, considering order?**

Good for names.

### Jaro-Winkler

> **Jaro + bonus for same prefix**

```text
MARTHA
MARHTA
^^^^
prefix bonus
```

### Ukkonen

> **Don't calculate DP cells that cannot possibly matter**

```text
full matrix → narrow band
```

### Levenshtein automaton

> **Turn "distance ≤ k" into a finite-state machine.**

### Lucene

> **Intersect that fuzzy automaton with its dictionary FST.**

### BK-tree

> **Use triangle inequality to prune dictionary words.**

### SymSpell

> **Precompute deletes instead of generating all typo possibilities.**

### Norvig

> **Generate close candidates and choose the common one.**

### Noisy channel

> **Choose the candidate maximizing frequency × probability of the observed typo.**

[
\boxed{\hat c=\arg\max_c P(c)P(w|c)}
]

